# Workflow: artefact-ready

## Instruction

- Run a target using **Command** if no dependency found
- If target got failure, do not execute its parent target
- If a target has dependencies, run all of its dependency targets

## Inventory Directory

| OS Context | Path                            |
| ---------- | ------------------------------- |
| Windows    | `~/echo-home/windows`           |
| Mac OS     | `~/echo-home/workstation/macos` |
| Linux      | `~/echo-home`                   |

## DAG Definition

Complete target in DAG by executing **Command**

```Makefile
inventory:
    # Description: check if <package> exists inventory
    # Command: `cd <inventory_path>; cat .properd/artefacts.yaml`
    # Success: output show `package` name
    # Failure: output show no `package` name, workflow can be aborted immediately
check_sum:
    # Description: check if <package> has sha256sum verified
    # Command: `.function/artefacts`
    # Success: output shows <package> OK
    # Failure: output shows <package> not OK or missing
download: check_sum inventory
    # Description: download
    # Command: `.function/artefact-geti <package>`
    # Success: no error found in output
    # Failure: error found in output 
    # Input: [check_sum] must be in failure or [inventory] must be in success
deploy: check_sum download
    # Description: install package into system
    # Command: `.function/artefact-readi <package>`
    # Success: no error found in output
    # Failure: error found in output
    # Input: rerun [check_sum], [download] can be ignore when rerun of [check_sum] succeeds
```
